  "question": {
    "text": "If $\\lim _{x \\rightarrow 1} \\frac{(5 x+1)^{1 / 3}-(x+5)^{1 / 3}}{(2 x+3)^{1 / 2}-(x+4)^{1 / 2}}=\\frac{\\mathrm{m} \\sqrt{5}}{\\mathrm{n}(2 \\mathrm{n})^{2 / 3}}$, where $\\operatorname{gcd}(\\mathrm{m}, \\mathrm{n})=1$, then $8 \\mathrm{~m}+12 \\mathrm{n}$ is equal to______",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "100",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & \\lim _{x \\rightarrow 1} \\frac{\\frac{1}{3}(5 x+1)^{-2 / 3} 5-\\frac{1}{3}(x+5)^{-2 / 3}}{\\frac{1}{2}(2 x+3)^{-1 / 2} \\cdot 2-\\frac{1}{2}(x+4)^{-1 / 2}} \\\\ & =\\frac{8}{3} \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{6^{2 / 3}} \\begin{array}{l}m=8 \\\\ n=3\\end{array} \\\\ & 8 m+12 n=100\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
